cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "immunerepertoire: shared core for reproducible immune repertoire and single-cell analysis"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below, together with the methods listed in docs/references.md."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Sbihi"
    given-names: "Zineb"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6695-7695"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ZinebSBIHI/immune-repertoire-pipelines"
license: MIT
version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-10-21"
keywords:
  - immunology
  - AIRR
  - T-cell receptor
  - B-cell receptor
  - repertoire sequencing
  - single-cell RNA-seq
  - somatic hypermutation
  - clonal expansion
  - antigen specificity
  - reproducible research
  - R
abstract: >-
  An R package holding the shared methods of three configuration-driven
  pipelines for adaptive immune receptor repertoires (bulk and single-cell,
  T-cell and B-cell receptors) and single-cell gene expression: clonotype
  definition, diversity at a common sequencing depth, differential clonal
  abundance against a within-subject baseline with category and significance
  kept apart, clone tracking, CDR3 physicochemistry and networks,
  convergence against a permutation null, paired statistics at small sample
  size, specificity annotation against public receptor references, B-cell
  clonal inference, hypermutation, selection and lineage, receptor embedding
  joined to the transcriptome, and single-cell expression QC, clustering and
  markers. Every analysis is driven by one validated configuration file, and
  every run records its parameters and package versions beside its outputs.
